{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"The completion verifier receives only the fenced ticket_context (description + comments, gate_ops.py assemble step) — zero file contents. Every file is discovered agentically: measured across today's five verifier runs, 84-158 requests x ~4-6s each, dominated by read_file/search_files round-trips, and all four captured runaway loops were search_files repeat signatures — the model hunting for text it expects to exist. Wall-clock cost is round-trips, not tokens: runs already cache-read 8.7M of 8.8M input tokens, but that history was assembled one tool round-trip at a time.\n\nDesign (operator-ratified direction): PRE-FETCH, do not restrict. Append a bounded, clearly-labelled prefetched-content section to the verifier context — starting with the ticket's declared file_impact files and the referencing commits' diffs (git show of trailer commits) — while keeping the full tool surface untouched so the agent can still explore beyond the prefetch. Assistance, not a ceiling.\n\nPhase 0 — measure first: extend the aec1 usage recorder to log the raw distinct fetch list per gate run — (tool, path/query) — not just hashed top-repeats. Today's records cannot validate the overlap hypothesis: signatures hash full args (line ranges, query strings), and brute-forcing 2,573 tracked paths resolved only 2 of 6 heavy read_file repeats. Record first; tune the prefetch set from measurement.\n\nPhase 1 — prefetch file_impact + referencing-commit diffs, bounded (per-file char cap and an aggregate cap mirroring completion_recovery's _MAX_* pattern; oversize files truncated with an explicit marker naming the tool call to fetch the rest). Same lever for the per-criterion recovery evidence runs (completion_recovery.py ~:517), which currently re-explore the same files independently.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Phase 0: every agentic gate run records its distinct fetch list (tool name + primary path/query arg) in the usage log by default; checked by a unit test asserting the recorded shape for a run with known tool calls.\n- [ ] Overlap measurement exists: a small analysis entry point (script or subcommand) reports the fraction of recorded fetches covered by a ticket's file_impact; checked by running it on recorded data.\n- [ ] Phase 1: the completion verifier's context includes a labelled prefetch section with file_impact file contents and referencing-commit diffs, bounded per-file and in aggregate; unit test pins the assembly (bounds, truncation marker, label).\n- [ ] The tool surface is unchanged: the verifier retains read_file/search_files/list_directory; unit test pins the toolset with prefetch enabled.\n- [ ] Recovery evidence runs receive the same prefetch section; unit test.\n- [ ] Live Bedrock A/B before ship (session experiment, not in unit suite): a verifier-scale run on a real closed ticket's material with prefetch vs the recorded baselines (84-158 requests) reduces total request count by at least 20% versus the recorded baseline for the same ticket, and the verdict class (PASS/FAIL) equals the baseline run's verdict class; both request counts and both verdicts recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean; full CI marker suite matches the pre-existing baseline.\n\n## Testing\nHeld-out unit oracle for context assembly + toolset pins (`python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/ -q`). Phase-0 recorder shape test alongside existing usage_log tests. Live A/B on Bedrock recorded as ticket comments with usage-log figures."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785991622256655001,"uuid":"e74a00e5-bc61-4e01-9b47-f1ced8dd1bfb"}